{
	"name": "Catastropic Failure",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/environment/wilderness/terrain-rocks-brown.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 13th level, your environment becomes as much a tool in your ambush as your firearm. If you have 1 minute to prepare for an ambush, you can create an explosive device using 5 firearm ammunition rounds to fell a tree, create a rockslide, or bust open a water tank or other massive container. As an action on your turn after the first round of combat, you can trigger the explosive to create an area of difficult terrain that is a 20ft cube. Any creature within that area must make a perception check against your combat maneuver DC or you can treat them as surprised for your @UUID[Compendium.a5e-martial-artistry.class-features.Item.UEkwAVUB2p10lU8T]{Get The Drop} ability on your next turn.</p><p>If the explosive goes unused, you can reclaim the ammunition.</p>",
